# H13 query 8 — "Which later decisions depended on that outcome?"
#
# Interpretation (docs/adr referenced from docs/experiment/implementation-notes.md
# Phase 6 section): a decision D's OBSERVED_SUCCESS outcome changes the real
# world state of whatever domain object D concerned (e.g. a work order's
# shortage/at_risk flips critical -> mitigated). A "later decision that
# depended on that outcome" is one that concerns the SAME domain object
# (oo:concernsWorkOrder is the traversable link — spec 05's "typed fac:
# object references") and was created AFTER D. This is the same-work-order
# causal-adjacency interpretation, not a claim of provenance/evidence-level
# dependency (which would need each LATER decision to have cited D's
# specific evidence snapshot — not modeled at that granularity in v1).
#
# Phase 9 step 0b: TWO graph scopes, not one — this query, unlike q1-q7,
# genuinely spans two different decisions' own named graphs (the anchor
# decision D and each later decision that shares D's oo:concernsWorkOrder
# object, which is itself a shared fac:WorkOrder node by design — that
# fan-OUT across decisions is the whole point of the query, not a bug to
# scope away). The anchor is bound to its own graph via %%GRAPH_IRI%%
# (known up front from the caller's decision_id, same substitution q1-q7
# use). Each candidate later decision is scoped via GRAPH ?laterGraph — a
# VARIABLE, not a literal — so every pattern inside that block (including
# the ?actorNode oo:actorId ?laterActor join, the same shared-node shape
# q5's fix addresses) is forced to resolve within that ONE later decision's
# own graph, never fanning out across every OTHER graph that actor/work
# order was ever referenced in.
PREFIX oo: <https://example.local/oo/>
SELECT DISTINCT ?laterDecisionId ?laterCreatedAt ?laterStatus ?laterActor WHERE {
  GRAPH <%%GRAPH_IRI%%> {
    ?decision oo:decisionId "%%DECISION_ID%%" ;
              oo:createdAt ?createdAt ;
              oo:concernsWorkOrder ?workOrder .
  }
  GRAPH ?laterGraph {
    ?laterDecision oo:concernsWorkOrder ?workOrder ;
                   oo:decisionId ?laterDecisionId ;
                   oo:createdAt ?laterCreatedAt ;
                   oo:status ?laterStatusConcept .
    OPTIONAL { ?laterDecision oo:actor ?actorNode . ?actorNode oo:actorId ?laterActor . }
  }
  BIND(STRAFTER(STR(?laterStatusConcept), "https://example.local/oo/") AS ?laterStatus)
  FILTER(?laterCreatedAt > ?createdAt)
}
ORDER BY ?laterCreatedAt
